{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1134783-seemings-as-narrative-turning-point","id":1134783,"title":"Seemings as Narrative Turning Point","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-28T01:32:26-07:00","id":1134783,"title":"Seemings as Narrative Turning Point","content":"In 2E previews of David's Seeming was a way you run away from your Keeper, end of story. In 2E Rose's version Seeming can be this - but also 'curse' putted on by the Keeper on you. Or your way to find peace on Earth, once you escaped.<br /> <br /> Last few days I have wondered on interesting ( I hope ) theory on this idea - <b>That (final) 2E Seeming are Narrative Turning Point for changelings lives. </b>If most important event to character was her way to free herself from Keeper - then in that instance Seeming is established for her. If it was Keeper laying 'curse' on changeling ( like Enchantress changing Prince into Beast in <b>'Beauty and the Beast'</b> ), then Seeming for changeling is set then. And if characters return to Earth without Seeming till then, it's determined how she was coping with hazards of Hedge on her way back - as her journey from Hedge to Earth was most important event.<br /> <br /> Just theory, but sounds as it works with spoiled information.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-28-2017, 06:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T02:01:41-07:00","id":1134786,"title":"","content":"Your title had me thinking that it was another developer preview <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T04:53:19-07:00","id":1134801,"title":"","content":"It certainly works with the Grimm Seeming from <b>A Grimm Dark Era</b>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1426-aberranteyes","name":"AberrantEyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1426_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T05:09:45-07:00","id":1134803,"title":"","content":"I imagine that like 1/3 of all 2E changelings have CHOSEN their Seeming by defying their Keeper and - literally - <i>choosing their story </i>- like Fairest leading small revolt in Arcadia. Then second 1/3 are those that Keeper 'cursed' or modeled to be their Seemings - like 'immoral Fairest', made to be vain by Keeper, like his Gentry 'little princess'. And the rest of 1/3 are those that 'simply run away', when Keeper was not looking - they can be Seemingless if they not change their story till they come to the Earth. I think this is where most Grimms can come, as they are from times where Keepers en masse have more important problems ( change of Contracts and Pledges ) than looking for their servants. As changeling did not do something truly defining it's next story - he do not have Seeming chosen, yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T14:05:26-07:00","id":1134941,"title":"","content":"this might not be what Rose was going for, but I love it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T09:19:04-07:00","id":1135176,"title":"","content":"This is likely how I'll play it out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"atta